<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad Ali Khan Wallajah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1717–1795</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Muhammad Ali Wallajah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad Ali Khan Wallajah was Nawab of the Carnatic from 1749 to 1795. Backed by the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> against his French-supported rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanda-sahib">Chanda Sahib</a>, he won the throne through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carnatic-wars">Carnatic Wars</a>, which included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-clive">Robert Clive</a>'s defence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcot">Arcot</a> in 1751. He moved his court to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Madras</a>, but heavy debts to the Company and its servants left him ever more dependent on the British.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-khan-wallajah.jpg" alt="Muhammad Ali Khan Wallajah" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Smart · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Muhammad_%27Ali_Khan,_Nawab_of_Arcot_and_Prince_of_the_Carnatic_(1718-1795)_(by_John_Smart).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
